<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">Justification for Changes in Theatre BA Curriculum</h2>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    These changes are a proactive response to the addition of new faculty and the concomitant growth of the program in student numbers and facilities. The curriculum now reflects classes more suitable to a BA in Theatre—including new classes in design, performance, dramaturgy, and video production. Required courses, both core and tracks, align with peer and aspirant peer theatre programs. The focus on experiential learning and entrepreneurship distinguishes the UAH program from our peers, becoming a point of regional prominence.
  </p>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
    Likewise, elective courses have expanded to meet the needs of students to become employable in their chosen field once they graduate. The electives allow students to deepen their knowledge in a particular area, or broaden their experience into a larger range of fields within theatre.
  </p>
</div>

